# Su Wen, Chapter 1 — 上古天真論篇第一

**English translation for the series.** *Shàng Gǔ Tiān Zhēn Lùn* — "Discourse on
the Natural Purity of High Antiquity."

> A dramatized adaptation of a classical philosophical text. Not medical advice.
> Nothing in this chapter is a treatment, a dosage or a diagnosis, and nothing
> below should be read as one.

## About this translation

The source is the received classical text of Su Wen Chapter 1, compiled around
the Han period and long in the **public domain**. **This English rendering is
original work made for this series**, not a reproduction of any published
translation, and the requested source page (`8bei8.com`) is unreachable from the
repo host — the agent proxy denies the domain — so nothing here derives from that
site's own modern commentary.

It is deliberately **plain rather than literary**. The series' arguments turn on
hedges and conditionals that smoother translations often drop — 余聞 *"I have
heard"*, 其知道者 *"those who knew the Way"*, 有極時 *"there is a limit"* — so those
are rendered explicitly even where it costs elegance.

Technical terms are left transliterated where English has no honest equivalent
(*qi*, *yin/yang*, *tian gui*) and glossed on first use. Bracketed words are
supplied for sense and are not in the Chinese.

