## 4. The body's schedule — sevens and eights

The Emperor asked whether the loss of the ability to have children is a matter of
age, or of exhausted vitality. Qi Bo answered by counting.

### Women, in sevens

> 女子七歲，腎氣盛，齒更髮長。

*At **seven**, a girl's kidney qi flourishes; her milk teeth are replaced and her
hair grows long.*

> 二七而天癸至，任脈通，太衝脈盛，月事以時下，故有子。

*At **fourteen** the **tian gui** arrives — the maturing capacity to reproduce —
the Conception vessel opens, the Penetrating vessel flourishes, the monthly
courses come in their season, and she can bear children.*

> 三七，腎氣平均，故真牙生而長極。

*At **twenty-one**, kidney qi is level and even; the wisdom teeth come in and
growth reaches its full extent.*

> 四七，筋骨堅，髮長極，身體盛壯。

*At **twenty-eight**, sinews and bones are firm, the hair is at its fullest, and
the body is at its strongest.*

> 五七，陽明脈衰，面始焦，髮始墮。

*At **thirty-five**, the yangming vessel declines; the face begins to wither and
the hair begins to fall.*

> 六七，三陽脈衰於上，面皆焦，髮始白。

*At **forty-two**, the three yang vessels decline in the upper body; the face
withers throughout and the hair begins to whiten.*

> 七七，任脈虛，太衝脈衰少，天癸竭，地道不通，故形壞而無子也。

*At **forty-nine**, the Conception vessel is empty and the Penetrating vessel
diminished; the tian gui is exhausted, the earthly passage no longer opens, and
so the body alters and she no longer bears children.*

### Men, in eights

> 丈夫八歲，腎氣實，髮長齒更。

*At **eight**, a boy's kidney qi is solid; his hair grows and his milk teeth are
replaced.*

> 二八，腎氣盛，天癸至，精氣溢瀉，陰陽和，故能有子。

*At **sixteen**, kidney qi flourishes, the tian gui arrives, essence-qi overflows,
yin and yang are in accord, and he can father children.*

> 三八，腎氣平均，筋骨勁強，故真牙生而長極。

*At **twenty-four**, kidney qi is level and even, sinews and bones are strong;
the wisdom teeth come in and growth reaches its full extent.*

> 四八，筋骨隆盛，肌肉滿壯。

*At **thirty-two**, sinews and bones are at their height and the flesh is full
and strong.*

> 五八，腎氣衰，髮墮齒槁。

*At **forty**, kidney qi declines; the hair falls and the teeth grow dry.*

> 六八，陽氣衰竭於上，面焦，髮鬢頒白。

*At **forty-eight**, yang qi is exhausted in the upper body; the face withers and
the hair at the temples turns grey.*

> 七八，肝氣衰，筋不能動，天癸竭，精少，腎藏衰，形體皆極。

*At **fifty-six**, liver qi declines and the sinews can no longer move freely;
the tian gui is exhausted, essence is scant, the kidney organ weakens, and the
body reaches its limit throughout.*

> 八八，則齒髮去。

*At **sixty-four**, the teeth and hair are gone.*

