## 5. The exception, and the ceiling

The Emperor observed that some old men still father children, and asked how.

Qi Bo answered that such a man's natural endowment exceeded the ordinary, his qi
passages remained open, and his kidney qi was in surplus. But he added a limit:

> 此雖有子，男不過盡八八，女不過盡七七，而天地之精氣皆竭矣。

*"Even so, a man does not exceed the full eight eights, nor a woman the full seven
sevens, before the essence-qi of heaven and earth is exhausted in them."*

The Emperor asked whether one who follows the Way can still reach a hundred and
bear children. Qi Bo replied that one who follows the Way can hold off ageing and
keep the body whole — and such a person may still bear children even when old.

