## 6. Four kinds of people

> 上古有真人者，提挈天地，把握陰陽，呼吸精氣，
> 獨立守神，肌肉若一，故能壽敝天地，無有終時。

*"In high antiquity there were **True Men**, who took up heaven and earth and held
yin and yang in their grasp, who breathed the essence-qi, who stood alone guarding
the spirit, whose flesh was as one — and so their years outwore heaven and earth
and had no ending."*

> 中古之時，有至人者，淳德全道，和於陰陽，調於四時，
> 去世離俗，積精全神…亦歸於真人。

*"In middle antiquity there were **Perfected Men** of pure inner power and whole
Way, in harmony with yin and yang and attuned to the four seasons, who left the
age and departed from custom, gathering essence and keeping the spirit whole …
these too return to the condition of the True Men."*

> 其次有聖人者，處天地之和，從八風之理，適嗜欲於世俗之間，
> 無恚嗔之心…形體不敝，精神不散，亦可以百數。

*"Next there were **Sages**, who dwelt in the harmony of heaven and earth,
followed the pattern of the eight winds, fitted their appetites to the customs of
the world, and held no anger in their hearts … their bodies did not wear out, their
spirit did not scatter, and they too could be counted in hundreds [of years]."*

> 其次有賢人者，法則天地，象似日月，辨列星辰，逆從陰陽，
> 分別四時，將從上古合同於道，**可使益壽而有極時**。

*"Next there were **Worthy Men**, who took heaven and earth as their model, who
took the sun and moon as their image, who distinguished the stars in their
courses, who followed the movement of yin and yang and separated out the four
seasons; who looked back to high antiquity and brought themselves into accord with
the Way. **These may increase their years — but there is a limit.**"*

**Note.** The four kinds descend: the True Man is placed beyond reach in a remote
past; the Sage lives in the world and is credited only with a long ordinary life;
and of the most attainable kind the chapter states its own ceiling — 有極時,
*"there is a limit."* The text bounds its own strongest claim, in its own voice.

